# Run outputs are not tracked — result JSON, summary/fold CSVs, figures, .npz
# arrays and executed notebooks all live here and belong on the filesystem.
#
# What IS tracked is the small text that explains and reproduces a run: its
# README.md (the thing that actually preserves the finding), its submit.sh, and
# any script that lives with it under the project's "per-experiment scripts live
# with their run" rule.
#
# Allowlist, so a new output format cannot leak in by default.
*
!*/
!.gitignore
!*.md
!*.sh
!*.py
